Z||000007||JSocha||10-03-2001||09:58 AM||||KEN, you ARE still around!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Haven't heard much from you lately... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> of course, come to think of it, haven't heard much from myself either...hmmmmmm?<P>Anyways, how you are you doing?  How are things over your direction?  Is at least some sort of normalacy starting to set back in to the/your lives over in NY?<P>I realize that is a strange question to ask and possibly very difficult to answer, but hoping all my best for NY and its people to recover and heal, even if it is a little bit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Take care my friend!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>SC/yo_sweet, why?  Just why? Besides the gf reason you gave?<P>Now I will have to go into name translation mode:  yo_sweet use to be Santa_cruzer seven times removed and prior to gf pet name conflicts after.......etc.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||10-03-2001||10:20 AM||||Its amazing how far the WTC thing reaches out. Rochester is 400 miles from NYC on the highway, but even here:<P> we have been sending paramedics, firemen, and state troopers to NYC for 1 week shifts.<P> my company, Xerox, did loose some people in the towers, they were working on, or installing equipment at a couple of customer sites.<P> My daughters BF works in the ER of St Marys Hosp, i think its in brooklin. He use to be a paramedic, so when the first tower was hit, they pulled him off his job (admissions) and sent him down there. He got there just in time to flee from the second collaspe.<P>  some of his best friends were firemen on the first truck to respond, they were killed - its been very hard on him.<P>  and even little things. When I take my HobieCat out on lake Ontario, the Coast Guard Crews from station Rochester are always out patrolling on the lake now.+<P> something Ive been thinking about, I want to share it with him next time I see him - I really believe the people working in the WTC were murdered - but I would not say that about the firemen, paramedics, or policemen.<P>  rescue teams have very detailed information on all buildings in their districts. The WTC towers were designed to remain standing for a max of two hours with a fire burning out of control.<P> the rescue workers KNEW that. They knew the towers were going to collaspe. They knew there were still people in there. They made a conscience decision to keep going back in, they knew they would not be able to get everyone out before they collasped.<P> In other words, they knew they were going to keep going back in and pulling people out and the only thing that was going to stop them was the towers falling on them.<P> When I was in the coast guard our unofficial motto was "you have to go out, you dont have to come back".<P> I dont think this has been pointed out clearly in the media. Those rescue workers were not murdered. They knowingly, consciencely, and willingly gave their lives to save others. They knew they were gonna die in there.<P> In the words of the good book, "Nobody takes my life from me. I lay my life down".<P> I think that should be inscribed on a memorial for the fallen rescue workers in NYC.||||reg||10
